  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_b72cf18b0b53484c8e9a741d1c940f6d",
      "statement": "The runner is a state machine expressed as a transition table that the loop executes, and the successor lookup raises on a pair it has no edge for, so the loop can take no path the table does not contain.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/loop.py#L16-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5afc7030d7e85243d8eaf7af33e1fe3b1e31440d3fd29dbf5ee39ff42b61c9cd:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/triage.py#L318-L333",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5fff095fa4a09b3d35a7278bd7e6fa35d3ce45f3c21fd658daf434e286afaf4b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_36d37ba18ec34c2e92f235efc1018033",
      "statement": "The safeguard requiring the uncertain pool to be drained before widening scope is enforced by the absence of an edge rather than by ordering in code: widening is reachable only through the drain state, so no later edit can reorder it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/triage.py#L352-L372",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:13312d80aa6970688dd8f8901b4af3a8eae5503ac3e0c40ebddd64f1153eba83:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3991d7dc49194225a221eb1eb82579d0",
      "statement": "One transition exists so the vision branch is reachable from the end of the ladder as well as from a descent that found nothing, because a triage that rejects every offered row would otherwise abstain while an unreadable page sits unexamined.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/loop.py#L25-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1eef44982acd014d00fbfd953dce33ac27461ee16d727edb28e3797deee98f35:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_230ab815948843dc8e94f9d18ae5e8d3",
      "statement": "The loop's signals are observations it can make for free from an envelope it already has, so no signal requires a call that was not going to happen anyway.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/triage.py#L334-L351",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1c2f076fc7fd0316428fce1f547334e629a2bc29d18b9e109a383db06fa94ede:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_90a8f7f972694402af63298a3885099a",
      "statement": "A move ceiling bounds the loop and exceeding it raises rather than abstaining, because failing to reach a terminal state is a bug rather than an answer.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/loop.py#L216-L218",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f2e1c071418e2a53bcd75f914fba0ca301f0e1245912365c2dd9fe31baf0f066:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/loop.py#L73-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:37d98f8dcc8984b48d980916d86b849a6666de89c58fb720c637b4a44e8b1f10:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c416042f6df54ee49542d33efb251822",
      "statement": "The loop holds no state between questions — it is created per question and discarded, scope and exclusions are parameters, nothing is module-level or cached — so two replicas answering the same question make the same moves.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/loop.py#L31-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:104e8b4f84198ef1c7eae768fe3fc4c9b8957a52603adddbff95293d1b889da2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cc244c0381594d41a3598b783a81f1a6",
      "statement": "Every tool call the runner makes goes through the caller's dispatcher rather than to a tool function directly, so the runner is a caller of the eight tools and never a ninth path into them.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/loop.py#L37-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c074e0ba0c30836df86e589274987dd4fdf9029669c69cdefdcf3e83a26494c6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_852ef0c20fc7455abc181ecc510f9a9d",
      "statement": "An outage, an exhausted quota or an unusable model answer ends the loop as a typed refusal carrying the tool's own status and code rather than as an abstention, because an outage rendered as \"not found\" is the service's failure delivered as the caller's confidence.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/loop.py#L43-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b170a5b491ad215d72b966bd68c0570f63c80746302853e85324a4dad608faf9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_654adb61a6454a9a8a5ea17318e32acb",
      "statement": "Triage marks every candidate from its summary row for free before any spend, reading only four fields already present — summary, matching surfaces, grounded rate and text trust — and calling no model, opening no raster and embedding nothing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/triage.py#L1-L8",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c5ea5720832801f8b8bd77bf96d149e2d1bb72fb5ddbc5ef998336b6d2e1921f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_88a77c8125af4dbf8433d00531ca803c",
      "statement": "Triage is tri-state rather than binary because a keep/drop decision discards the fallback pool, leaving a fresh search as the only repair for a wrong drop — the uncertain pool makes an insufficient read cost one more look rather than one more search.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/triage.py#L10-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a5e8f49566a0067c8662540adb83ae5a3881baffe36dc6ad49fea26c9bf0af1b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/triage.py#L47-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d61994139979dbaf9c62bdb149f8794c678973029456c69ebeb8cdddb3eccbbe:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9057e107b8b34bf2bc9238fe0504e9bb",
      "statement": "Every triage judgement errs toward carrying a candidate forward, because a needlessly uncertain page costs a place in a pool drained only on failure while a wrongly irrelevant page produces an abstention on a corpus that contained the answer.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/triage.py#L20-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bfeee9fd3323985fc121f7c2f06fc3ee0041f012fd253f02d4e22ea40ec20fa9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c717151260f44ceba8b9c98ebff57d76",
      "statement": "Each triage mark carries exactly one reason from a closed list, because a reason nothing sets is a column a reviewer cannot act on.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/triage.py#L58-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f7adb7cba27da10495aab8d6f1632001afd1b6523eee9aa04995345ed42f1c04:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c1ba5ea8578b4ab7bfc6f07e656fb3e7",
      "statement": "The five safeguards are a single definition read twice — the triage module holds the text and enforces it, and the prompt module prints it — because two statements of a rule stay the same rule only when there is one statement.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/prompt.py#L1-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6f53834626c7c8aee29c1b8cb586da9e345db412e0baedd8cefcb36ee45de699:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/triage.py#L13-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:52caf0c790e45d88eb5a360485e1e7931e9d4f7c8144382943d16c7ccb3f3900:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/triage.py#L95-L111",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:20ee5e86d15633ccdfc0e1aff2990d4762e2af79c8137940f8fbdb22e1e98f47:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e0dbc2bf3ce045dda8bc275bf6d2e728",
      "statement": "Nothing in triage performs matching: term overlap with a summary decides whether to look, never whether a code is printed on a page, and a triage mark can never reach a response as a hit, a citation or a claim.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/triage.py#L27-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fc80fd8917b7fae1808b85d06549a67668ed341680edad857cf20a2be44c63c3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a50e7d58b24d49d695c50003b72e578a",
      "statement": "The route between the free look and the paid read is chosen for free before either call with no model call of its own, and defaults to the free route — the paid one is for a caller that cannot see or whose context cannot hold another raster.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/route.py#L1-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0f91c089e91e42d90ca4f47775bed4ba30101acb703752b2038e5321e745d8a7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dc71497ad82e44c19f0524c6dab747fb",
      "statement": "The automatic per-code stamping lives inside the paid read, so on the free route the agent has read codes off a raster with nothing checking them — which is precisely why the answer gate is server-side and unconditional, and why a route decision is never a trust decision.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/route.py#L23-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:334fa49d383838ba64485d9819c8d35f46f52f4ed09ab85e9b9792745240b87b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3ca565f0cfc748a59b34b80c77244cc1",
      "statement": "Whether the caller can see is a property of the caller rather than of the deployment, so it arrives as an argument and no session remembers a previous call's capability.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/route.py#L31-L34",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:82755344708dc1f2b0d28fb506506acac7c85898da33a97ed90e70bc1ab0a356:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_03bdab8324fb40c2812b57e4608822be",
      "statement": "The answer gate runs one verify per (claim, page) pair and folds the verdicts, so the call log answers whether a code was checked against the page it is cited on rather than whether it was checked somewhere.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/answer.py#L333-L365",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bde733b781202200d6b80ef674754029c28a242a7f74f9b9a93e8b82e8abde69:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_464c23199f3d4dd7bf9489b86426108f",
      "statement": "The gate is unconditional with no flag to skip it, does not ask which route produced the draft, and re-checks the stamps a paid read already applied rather than trusting them.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/answer.py#L9-L17",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1dbc7fbca0e9ccf1ff00d6afaf3c3a0dd5efed01c48974c082a37c75abe4c4a5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5366d2dd98294542a882f19eb4e08e01",
      "statement": "A claim cited on no page is a rejection, because a code asserted over nothing has nothing to verify it against; and a verifier that fails raises rather than producing an absence.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/answer.py#L350-L362",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4c92235068feef0f1207af7ada2dfe053fe340334c860be71aefff1bddcd1fd5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5dcc72cf3d22417cb8616f46588edf15",
      "statement": "A rejected draft returns no prose and never echoes the rejected code — only the page and the observed tokens present instead — because putting the misread code where a person is reading for an answer is one style change away from rendering it as the answer; the gate logs the distribution rather than the codes for the same reason.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/answer.py#L25-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3edcbbfef0135a053423455e29eaac963c3a61b20df87270e911ebdcfb13acb7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/answer.py#L377-L383",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4fbeba21e9667d982abe6c792ef8f736f98e7e5c06bc1e631bd936807593390e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6d90388be0144c8e826a1d43b9ef51b2",
      "statement": "An abstention is composed from the coverage in three fixed clauses — what was done, the page and document counts, and the gap of unexamined image-only pages with the documents holding them — rather than selected from a list of sentences.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/answer.py#L495-L521",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:da0b9507065d525720494e8b97f37bd41c83eb215439908092a9a636f9ff14c8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_22804c840d4e4bd5a9401ee71d4df3d5",
      "statement": "The phrase asserting absence from the documents is a named constant forbidden while unexamined image-only pages remain, and the check runs on the composed string rather than on the branch that produced it, so a later edit adding a reassuring closing sentence is caught by the same line.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/answer.py#L393-L396",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1a22f414211282b760622e05d96c780dbf3561cbd76d08988e3924feddc9fabe:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/answer.py#L548-L560",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ad92821b5f559c3acc823120a25c98005b0f6d4240c0076f887f27ece2352734:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8e4a5eef891b48eeb43693b7b7279c2f",
      "statement": "When no page was searched at all the abstention says so and draws no conclusion about the corpus, because a completeness claim over zero pages is the same fabricated absence arrived at from the other end.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/answer.py#L521-L534",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5bd1ca7c1f1e4655ec49f97da0bf04d1bd33a9ab45c87e4886c5f16e369b04b4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cbd0d65519534d46b307a5c0d6292e19",
      "statement": "The system prompt is deterministic by construction — the same inputs render byte-identical text and its digest is over those bytes — because a prompt is a cache-key input wherever a released prompt reaches a paid call.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/prompt.py#L17-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aa6e6f6415b8edad1536abb9cd1699e459591e8b323136ee1612b27e11ce2471:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ee1f76289797469faaf056a1dc38b99a",
      "statement": "The runner prompt lives in Python with its own version label rather than as a digest-pinned packaged file, because it is composed per question from the tools a release serves and the budget in force, and sharing the extraction prompt's version label would re-key every frozen extraction response whenever a safeguard's wording changed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/runner/prompt.py#L23-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2144159a3fdffaa8ad56096e3026811030c008aff9c4202e2157e48ba9526466:"
        }
      ]
    }
